nodecode-agentpurse is a rewrite of maaz-bin-hassan's maaz-bin-hassan/agentpurse:

  https://github.com/maaz-bin-hassan/agentpurse
  commit 84a1ed7cc9dbac462a5bde8b65f6d105cc56b20b
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 MaAz Khan Hassan (LICENSE)

Rewritten: plugins/hermes, the Hermes plugin, as one Nodecode cell. Its twelve
MCP tools are twelve Lisp verbs in the purse: package, called through eval and
answering the server's own JSON; its /purse command is this cell's, with the
same budget, receipts, kill switch and resume, plus the pending purchase the
Hermes prompt used to hold; its JSON-RPC client is reimplemented on dexador with
the same rules (one session per call, reads retried, purchases never retried,
redirects refused, https or localhost only); its gate keeps the same blocks
(kill switch, blocked merchant, a guard block, the allowance, the per-session
limit, integer cents) and its one-time grants keep the same shape and ten-minute
ttl, in a JSON file under the home rather than in Hermes plugin state.

Left out: Hermes' own approval prompt and its `post_approval_response` hook,
which do not exist here. In their place a purchase asks the person watching
through nlk:ask-operator, and a shell that cannot answer a question (the TUI
alone) holds the purchase for /purse approve, typed by the person. Also left
out: the attendance classifier that reads Hermes' session environment variables
(here, no answering surface and no approval means nothing is sent, which is the
same fail-closed answer), the bundled skills/shop/SKILL.md as a skill file (its
rules are the primer and the tool descriptions), the catalog/ and DEMO.md, and
the Python tests, rewritten as this cell's own offline test.
